<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="0" dur="3.76">My name is Jared Isaacman. I am the</text><text start="1.76" dur="3.599">administrator of NASA. I get the</text><text start="3.76" dur="3.44">privilege of leading the world&amp;#39;s most</text><text start="5.359" dur="4.001">accomplished space agency during the</text><text start="7.2" dur="3.68">golden age of science and discovery. We</text><text start="9.36" dur="4.399">are going back to the moon. We&amp;#39;re here</text><text start="10.88" dur="4.56">with Artemis 3. They launch in 2027.</text><text start="13.759" dur="2.801">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We are so excited to represent America</text><text start="15.44" dur="3.44">and the American people.</text><text start="16.56" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Europe wants to be the strongest and</text><text start="18.88" dur="2.8">most reliable partner for the</text><text start="20.56" dur="2.16">exploration of the moon.</text><text start="21.68" dur="3.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We&amp;#39;re launching a bunch of different</text><text start="22.72" dur="4.639">rockets from the SLS to the Starship and</text><text start="25.6" dur="3.999">to the Blue Origin rocket. It&amp;#39;s going to</text><text start="27.359" dur="4.641">be fantastic. laying the groundwork for</text><text start="29.599" dur="4.64">the next phase of human exploration.</text><text start="32" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Our mission to launch next year shows</text><text start="34.239" dur="3.361">American leadership in space and the</text><text start="36" dur="5.2">Artemis program leading humans back to</text><text start="37.6" dur="8.2">the moon and onto Mars to lead humanity</text><text start="41.2" dur="4.6">and America in space.</text></transcript>